{%- liquid
  assign mock_orders = mock_orders_raw | split: ';'
  # Trim the list so a state can show the short table — under 11 orders there is no second page
  # and the control disappears entirely, which is its own thing to review.
  if orders_count
    assign mock_orders = mock_orders | slice: 0, orders_count
  endif
-%}

{%- capture crown -%}
  {%- comment -%} QA #8: the crown used a translate-y-[1px] nudge tuned against macOS font metrics,
    so it drifted again on Windows/Chrome. Two causes, both removed:
    1. The glyph spans y3..15 of the 20-box, i.e. its centre is 9 against the box centre 10 — the
       viewBox now starts at -1 so the artwork is centred in its own box, no nudge needed.
    2. items-center centred an 18px box inside a 25.2px line box, which also broke on a wrapped
       two-line benefit. The icon box is now exactly one line tall (see .wb-benefit-item__icon)
       and aligns to the first line, so the maths no longer depends on the font's metrics. {%- endcomment -%}
  <svg class="wb-benefit-item__icon shrink-0 text-gold" viewBox="0 -1 20 20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
    <path d="M2 6l3.5 3L10 3l4.5 6L18 6l-1.5 9h-13L2 6z"/>
  </svg>
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%} ---------- Welcome + Log Out ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%} QA #5: Log Out sits on the Welcome line (items-center), Kurdis 700 14px (Figma 1:337). {%- endcomment -%}
<div class="wb-welcome flex flex-col items-center text-center smd:!flex-row smd:!items-center smd:!text-left smd:!justify-between !gap-1">
  {%- comment -%} Membership tag sits above the last letter of the name, tilted (Figma). Spec: Kurdis Condensed ExtraBold 12px uppercase centered.
    QA #37: the tag used to be an inline-block INSIDE the centred h1, so its width was counted in the
    line box and pushed the name off-centre on mobile. It is now absolutely positioned off the end of
    an inline wrapper around the name — zero layout width, so the name centres on the real text. {%- endcomment -%}
  <h1 class="font-kurdis-condensed font-extrabold text-espresso text-[28px] md:!text-[36px] leading-none">
    <span class="relative inline-block">{{ 'customer.account.welcome' | t: first_name: fname }}
      {%- comment -%} Tilt is +4deg — the computed value must be `rotate: 4deg`. Written as
        rotate-[4deg] (NOT -rotate-[4deg], which Tailwind compiles to -4deg). This also matches
        Figma vector 1:380, which carries rotation +0.0696rad = +3.99°.
        Text #E4B850 on gold. {%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="absolute left-full bottom-full -ml-1 -mb-2 md:!-mb-3 rotate-[4deg] bg-gold text-[#E4B850] font-kurdis-condensed font-extrabold text-[12px] leading-none uppercase text-center whitespace-nowrap px-2 py-1 rounded-[6px] shadow-[2px_3px_4px_0px_rgba(0,0,0,0.2)]">{{ display_tier }}</span>
    </span>
  </h1>
  <a href="{{ routes.account_logout_url }}" class="wb-welcome__logout font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[14px] leading-none text-espresso hover-underline shrink-0">{{ 'customer.account.log_out' | t }}</a>
</div>

{%- comment -%} Worker load-failure note — hidden by default, shown when account.ts sets data-wb-error on the root {%- endcomment -%}
<p data-wb-error-note class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-semibold text-[12px] leading-[1.3] text-[#BD2121] mb-4" role="status">{{ 'customer.dashboard.load_error' | t }}</p>

{%- comment -%} ---------- Row 1: BOTH variants rendered; account.ts (renderSubscriptions) shows one
  by the worker's active_count — autoship is independent of tier. SSR shows the tier-guess as the
  initial paint / no-JS + error fallback. ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign guess_none = false -%}
{%- if autoship == 'none' -%}{%- assign guess_none = true -%}{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} Variant B — no autoship: wide credit block {%- endcomment -%}
<div data-wb-row-nocard{% unless guess_none %} data-wb-hide{% endunless %}>
  {%- comment -%} QA #40: this variant kept py-7 / !gap-5 and never got .wb-row1-card, so while the
    compact card was tightened to Figma this one stayed ~200px. Figma 1:739 draws the no-autoship
    mobile card as the same 350x162 box: 16 top, 88 content, 6 gap, 40 button, 12 bottom. Desktop
    keeps py-7 / gap-5 / min-h-120 — there the credit block and the button sit side by side. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%} Figma 1:602: this card is 774x104 with the button at y245-285, so 27px below it. {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="relative {{ card }} px-6 pt-4 pb-3 md:!pt-7 md:!pb-[27px] md:!px-5 mb-6 md:!min-h-[104px] flex flex-col !gap-1.5 md:!gap-5 md:!flex-row md:!items-center md:!justify-between">
    {%- comment -%} View Credit History pinned to the top-right in every state (short $0 or tall). {%- endcomment -%}
    <a href="{{ credit_history_url }}" class="absolute top-5 right-6 z-[1] font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-xs leading-none hover-underline text-espresso">{{ 'customer.dashboard.view_credit_history' | t }}</a>
    {%- comment -%} MOBILE: centered amount — matches the with-subscription (compact) card so both
      states look identical on mobile. Hidden on desktop. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%} QA #40/#27: Figma gives the mobile credit card an identical 350x162 box in BOTH
      states (1:739 no-autoship y254, 1:177 with-autoship y424). Card top → label 16px, → amount 30px,
      so the amount block sits 14px under the label row rather than being vertically centred with a
      +45px nudge (which is what made the card ~200px tall). The ~48px QA measured between
      "YOUR CREDIT:" and the amount falls out of the label's 24px inset + the card-centred amount. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="relative min-h-[88px] md:!hidden">
      <span class="absolute left-0 top-0 z-[1] rotate-[-1.99deg] opacity-90 font-gothic_condensed font-extrabold uppercase text-espresso text-[20px] leading-[1.04] max-w-[80px]">{{ 'customer.dashboard.your_credit' | t }}</span>
      <div class="flex flex-col items-center text-center pt-[14px]">
        <span class="font-kurdis-condensed font-extrabold text-[45px] leading-none text-dark-gold" data-wb-credit-balance>{{ credits_formatted }}</span>
        <div class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[10px] leading-none mt-[12px] text-dark-gold" data-wb-expiry-line>{{ 'customer.dashboard.expires_label' | t }} <span data-wb-credit-expiry>{{ credits_expiry }}</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    {%- comment -%} DESKTOP: label + amount inline on the left. Hidden on mobile. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="hidden md:!block flex-1">
      <div class="flex items-end !gap-3">
        <span class="inline-block origin-bottom-left rotate-[-4deg] font-gothic_condensed font-extrabold uppercase text-espresso text-[20px] leading-[0.95] max-w-[68px]">{{ 'customer.dashboard.your_credit' | t }}</span>
        <span class="font-kurdis-condensed font-extrabold text-[45px] leading-[0.78] text-dark-gold" data-wb-credit-balance>{{ credits_formatted }}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-xs leading-none mt-3 text-dark-gold" data-wb-expiry-line>{{ 'customer.dashboard.expires_label' | t }} <span data-wb-credit-expiry>{{ credits_expiry }}</span></div>
    </div>
    {%- comment -%} Redeem → on-page modal. Button class is ALWAYS the standard one (never touch it);
      the 335px desktop width lives on this wrapper, not the button. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%} Figma 1:602: the no-subscription card is 774x104 and its Redeem button is 335px
      — the same width as the button in the compact card, not a wider one. The old 470 was sized
      against the pre-774 container. Full-width when stacked. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="w-full shrink-0 md:w-[335px] md:!self-end">
      {%- render 'customer-credit-redeem', label: t_redeem, link: redeem_url, balance_formatted: credits_formatted, class: 'shadow-button !w-full !h-[40px] !text-[15px]' -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{%- comment -%} Variant A — has autoship: autoship card + compact credit {%- endcomment -%}
<div data-wb-row-autoship{% if guess_none %} data-wb-hide{% endif %}>
  {%- comment -%} Desktop gap 24px so the two cards land on Figma's 375 each inside the 774
    content column (774 - 24 = 750 / 2). Mobile keeps the tighter 16px stack gap. {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="flex flex-col md:!flex-row !gap-4 md:!gap-6 mb-4">

    {%- comment -%} Autoship card — active or cancelled. Filled by account.ts from Stay AI (worker). {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="wb-row1-card flex-1 {{ card }} p-5 md:p-6 flex flex-col" data-wb-autoship{% if is_cancelled %} data-wb-autoship-state="cancelled"{% endif %}>
      {%- comment -%} QA #29: Figma "Line 10" (y281, full 350 card width) puts a divider under the
        title row too, matching the bundle/line-item rows below. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="wb-autoship-title-row flex items-center justify-between">
        <span class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[12px] leading-none text-bear-black"
              data-wb-autoship-title
              data-wb-title-next="{{ 'customer.dashboard.next_autoship' | t }}"
              data-wb-title-prev="{{ 'customer.dashboard.previous_autoship' | t }}">{%- if is_cancelled -%}{{ 'customer.dashboard.previous_autoship' | t }}{%- else -%}{{ 'customer.dashboard.next_autoship' | t }}{%- endif -%}</span>
        {%- comment -%} Active-count badge (default) + Cancelled badge; account.ts shows one via
          data-wb-autoship-state. Count is empty in the real render (account.ts fills it) and
          pre-filled when the QA preview passes autoship_count. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- comment -%} The count badge points at the same Stay AI portal as "Manage Upcoming
          Orders" — it names the subscriptions, so it should open them too. Kept as the same element
          account.ts already fills via data-wb-autoship-count, just as an <a>. {%- endcomment -%}
        <a href="{{ manage_url }}" class="inline-flex items-center whitespace-nowrap shrink-0 min-w-[80px] h-[20px] px-[10px] rounded-[10px] font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[12px] leading-none text-espresso bg-sky-blue transition-opacity hover:opacity-80" data-wb-autoship-count data-wb-count-template="{{ 'customer.dashboard.active_autoships' | t: count: '__N__' }}">{%- if autoship_count != blank -%}{{ 'customer.dashboard.active_autoships' | t: count: autoship_count }}{%- endif -%}</a>
        <span class="wb-autoship-cancelled" data-wb-autoship-cancelled>{{ 'customer.dashboard.cancelled' | t }}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="wb-autoship-head flex items-baseline justify-between !gap-2">
        {%- comment -%} QA #25: bundle title is espresso #431A03 in Figma (mobile 1:1019 y286,
          desktop 1:24) — only the row label above it is #1B1B1B. {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[12px] leading-none text-espresso" data-wb-autoship-bundle>{{ autoship_bundle }}</span>
        <span class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[10px] leading-none whitespace-nowrap text-bear-black" data-wb-autoship-date-line>{{ 'customer.dashboard.next_shipment_label' | t }} <span data-wb-autoship-date>{{ autoship_next_date }}</span></span>
      </div>
      <ul class="flex flex-col mb-2" data-wb-autoship-items data-wb-more-template="{{ 'customer.dashboard.more_count' | t: count: '__N__' }}">
        {%- for item in autoship_items -%}
          {%- if item != blank -%}
          <li class="flex items-center justify-between !gap-2 font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[10px] leading-none text-[#955325]">
            <span>{{ item }}</span>
            {%- if forloop.last and autoship_more > 0 -%}
              <a href="{{ manage_url }}" class="hover-underline shrink-0 whitespace-nowrap text-[#955325]">{{ 'customer.dashboard.more_count' | t: count: autoship_more }}</a>
            {%- endif -%}
          </li>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
      {%- comment -%} Both CTAs are always rendered; CSS shows exactly one per data-wb-autoship-state
        (same mechanism as the badge and the next-shipment line). SSR can only guess the state, so
        rendering just one would leave a cancelled member — detected later by account.ts — looking at
        "Manage Upcoming Orders" instead of "Reactivate".

        Manage → Stay AI portal. SSR href = manage_url (settings.manage_autoship_url, defaulted to
        /apps/retextion, which auto-detects the logged-in member); account.ts overrides it with the
        worker's per-customer portal_url (Stay AI generate-portal-link token) when present. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div data-wb-autoship-manage class="mt-auto">
        {%- render 'wb-button', style: 'secondary-gold', label: t_manage, link: manage_url, class: 'shadow-button !w-full !h-[40px] !text-[15px]' -%}
      </div>
      {%- comment -%} Reactivate goes to the same Stay AI portal as Manage — reactivation happens
        there, and account.ts swaps in the per-customer portal_url for both. It must be a link, not
        a bare <button>: there is no reactivate endpoint in the theme to submit to. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div data-wb-autoship-reactivate class="mt-auto">
        {%- render 'wb-button', style: 'secondary-gold', label: t_reactivate, link: manage_url, class: 'shadow-button !w-full !h-[40px] !text-[15px]' -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} Compact credit card {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="wb-row1-card flex-1 {{ card }} p-5 md:p-6 flex flex-col justify-between">
      {%- comment -%} Layout: "Your Credit:" pinned left; amount centred horizontally and sitting
        14px under the label row (Figma 1:177 — card top → label 16, → amount 30); View Credit
        History top-right; expiry centred under the amount. QA #40: the old h-full/justify-center
        + translate-y hack pushed the card to ~200px against Figma's 162px. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="relative min-h-[88px] mb-[6px]">
        <a href="{{ credit_history_url }}" class="absolute right-0 top-0 z-[1] font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-xs leading-none hover-underline text-espresso">{{ 'customer.dashboard.view_credit_history' | t }}</a>
        <span class="absolute left-0 top-0 z-[1] rotate-[-1.99deg] opacity-90 font-gothic_condensed font-extrabold uppercase text-espresso text-[20px] leading-[1.04] max-w-[80px]">{{ 'customer.dashboard.your_credit' | t }}</span>
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center text-center pt-[14px]">
          <div class="font-kurdis-condensed font-extrabold text-[45px] leading-none text-dark-gold" data-wb-credit-balance>{{ credits_formatted }}</div>
          <div class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[10px] leading-none mt-[12px] text-dark-gold" data-wb-expiry-line>{{ 'customer.dashboard.expires_label' | t }} <span data-wb-credit-expiry>{{ credits_expiry }}</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      {%- render 'customer-credit-redeem', label: t_redeem, link: redeem_url, balance_formatted: credits_formatted, class: 'shadow-button !w-full !h-[40px] !text-[15px]' -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{%- comment -%} ---------- Row 2: Membership tier (+ Progress unless Elite) ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
<div class="{{ card }} p-5 md:!p-6 mb-4">
  <div class="flex flex-col {% unless is_elite %}md:!flex-row{% endunless %} !gap-4 md:!gap-6">

    {%- comment -%} Tier column {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="md:!flex-1 {% unless is_elite %}md:!pr-6{% endunless %}">
      <div class="flex items-start justify-between mb-1">
        {%- comment -%} Left column: label + tier stacked. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div>
          {%- comment -%} QA #3: card headings are #1B1B1B in Figma (1:346/1:356/1:626/1:635), not espresso. {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[12px] leading-none text-bear-black">{{ 'customer.dashboard.membership_tier' | t }}</span>
          {%- comment -%} QA #21: Figma tier heading is 25px (desktop 1:24 / 1:320, mobile 1:177 / 1:466). {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="font-kurdis-condensed font-extrabold text-gold text-[25px] leading-none mt-2">{{ display_tier }}</div>
        </div>
        {%- comment -%} Right column: membership action links. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="flex flex-col items-end !gap-2.5">
          {%- if is_elite -%}
            <a href="/community/membership?customerId={{ customer.id }}#change-plan" class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-xs leading-none hover-underline text-espresso">{{ 'customer.dashboard.change_tier' | t }}</a>
            <a href="/community/membership?customerId={{ customer.id }}" class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[10px] leading-none hover-underline text-espresso">{{ 'customer.dashboard.update_payment' | t }}</a>
          {%- endif -%}
          <a href="{{ membership_url }}" class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-xs leading-none hover-underline text-espresso">{{ 'customer.dashboard.membership_faq' | t }}</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      {%- comment -%} QA #38: mobile needs more air above this heading — see .wb-whats-included. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="wb-whats-included body font-bold text-bear-black mt-[15px] mb-[15px]">{{ 'customer.dashboard.whats_included' | t }}</div>
      {%- comment -%} QA #7: Figma Elite lays the 6 benefits out in COLUMNS (col1: $5 off + Earn $5;
        col2: Member exclusive + VIP CS; col3: Early access + Anniversary). grid-flow-col with 2 rows
        fills column-major from the same source order, and mobile (flex-col) keeps the list order. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%} Columns are sized to their content rather than to three equal thirds. With the
        content column at 774px, equal thirds leave 203px for the label while "Early access to sales
        and launches" needs 215, so it wrapped. max-content columns spread by space-between fit the
        real text (the widest column needs 215) and cannot wrap, whatever the copy. {%- endcomment -%}
      <ul class="flex flex-col {% if is_elite %}smd:!grid smd:!grid-flow-col smd:!grid-rows-2 smd:!grid-cols-[repeat(3,max-content)] smd:!justify-between{% endif %} !gap-x-6 !gap-y-2.5">
        {%- for benefit in benefits -%}
          <li class="wb-benefit-item flex items-start font-kurdis-semi-condensed text-espresso">{{ crown }}<span>{{ benefit }}</span></li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} Progress column (hidden for Elite) {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- unless is_elite -%}
      <div class="flex flex-col md:!flex-1 tier-divider">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between mb-3">
          <span class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[12px] leading-none text-bear-black">{{ 'customer.dashboard.progress_next_tier' | t }}</span>
          <a href="/community/membership?customerId={{ customer.id }}" class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-xs leading-none hover-underline text-espresso">{{ 'customer.dashboard.change_tier' | t }}</a>
        </div>
        <div class="font-kurdis-condensed font-extrabold text-gold text-[26px] leading-none mt-2 mb-3" data-wb-progress-tier>{{ next_tier_label }}</div>
        <div class="w-full h-[14px] rounded-full overflow-hidden mb-2" style="background-color: var(--color-brand-beige);">
          <div class="h-full rounded-full" style="width: {{ progress_percent }}%; background-color: var(--color-brand-gold);" data-wb-progress-bar></div>
        </div>
        <p class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-xs leading-none mb-4 text-espresso text-center"><span data-wb-progress-text>{{ progress_text }}</span>{% if display_tier == 'VIP' %} {{ 'customer.dashboard.progress_or_upgrade' | t }}{% else %} {{ 'customer.dashboard.progress_or' | t }} <a href="{{ membership_url }}" class="hover-underline">{{ 'customer.dashboard.progress_sign_up_autoship' | t }}</a>{% endif %}</p>

        <div class="membership-upsell">
          <p class="body font-bold text-bear-black mb-1">{{ 'customer.dashboard.upgrade_today' | t }} <span class="font-parslay text-gold">{{ 'customer.dashboard.why_wait' | t }}</span></p>
          <p class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-semibold text-[12px] leading-[1.2] text-center mb-3 text-bear-black">{{ 'customer.dashboard.elite_upsell_desc' | t }}</p>
          {%- comment -%} Upgrade to Elite = add the $25 Elite product to cart (settings.elite_product), reusing the shared elite add-to-cart snippet. {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- render 'elite-atc-button', label: t_upgrade, style: 'secondary-gold', class: 'shadow-button !w-full !h-[40px] !text-[15px]' -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- endunless -%}
  </div>
</div>

{%- comment -%} ---------- Order history ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
<div class="{{ card }} p-5 md:!p-6 mb-8">
  {%- comment -%} Header (title + timeframe) — hidden when the customer has no orders. The QA
    preview has no customer but does render a mock table, so it shows the header too. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if customer.orders.size > 0 or preview -%}
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between mt-2.5 mb-4 !gap-3">
    {%- comment -%} shrink-0: below ~360px the fixed-width timeframe squeezed this block and both
      headings wrapped to two lines. The timeframe compresses instead — see .wb-timeframe. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="shrink-0">
      {%- comment -%} QA #14/#31: the whole Order-History header is #1B1B1B in Figma (nodes read
        #000000 on 1:24 / 1:320 and mobile 1:177) — was espresso #431A03 on both breakpoints. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%} Figma: "Order History" = Kurdis SemiCondensed Bold 10px / 100%. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[10px] leading-none uppercase text-bear-black">{{ 'customer.dashboard.order_history' | t }}</div>
      {%- comment -%} Figma: "All Orders" = Tablet Gothic Condensed Extrabold 16px / 100%. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="font-gothic_condensed font-extrabold text-[16px] leading-none uppercase text-bear-black mt-2">{{ 'customer.dashboard.all_orders' | t }}</div>
    </div>
    {%- comment -%} Timeframe filter (Figma). TODO: wire to order filtering (JS/worker).
      QA #32: mobile gets a 175x36 r5 box (Figma "Rectangle 10511") — see .wb-timeframe.
      QA #49: the whole box has to be clickable, not just the <select>. The select is stretched
        over the entire control and made transparent, so a tap anywhere — including on the
        "Timeframe:" label and the padding — opens the native picker. The visible value is our own
        styled text, kept in sync by account.ts (data-wb-timeframe-value).
      QA #20: hover belongs to the label text only, not the dropdown value — see account.css. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="wb-timeframe relative flex items-center !gap-2 min-w-0">
      <span class="wb-timeframe__label font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[10px] leading-none text-center text-bear-black whitespace-nowrap">{{ 'customer.dashboard.timeframe' | t }}</span>
      <div class="inline-flex items-center !gap-1.5">
        {%- comment -%} QA #11: leading-none clips Kurdis ascenders in Chrome — give the line room. {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[10px] leading-[1.4] text-center text-bear-black whitespace-nowrap" data-wb-timeframe-value>Last 3 Months</span>
        <svg class="w-3 h-3 shrink-0 text-bear-black pointer-events-none" viewBox="0 0 12 8" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M1 1.5 6 6.5 11 1.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      </div>
      <select class="wb-timeframe__select absolute inset-0 w-full h-full opacity-0 cursor-pointer appearance-none" aria-label="{{ 'customer.dashboard.timeframe' | t | strip }}" data-wb-timeframe>
        <option>Last 3 Months</option>
        <option>Last 6 Months</option>
        <option>Last Year</option>
        <option>All Time</option>
      </select>
    </div>
  </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if customer.orders.size > 0 -%}
    {%- paginate customer.orders by 10 -%}
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full border-collapse wb-orders-table">
          {%- comment -%} QA #9/#10: rows = Kurdis 700 10px / 18px line (Figma 1:365), whole table #1B1B1B. {%- endcomment -%}
          <thead>
            <tr class="text-left tag text-bear-black uppercase">
              <th class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/20">{{ 'customer.dashboard.col_order' | t }}</th>
              <th class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/20">{{ 'customer.dashboard.col_date' | t }}</th>
              <th class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/20">{{ 'customer.dashboard.col_tracking' | t }}</th>
              <th class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/20 hidden md:!table-cell">{{ 'customer.dashboard.col_payment' | t }}</th>
              <th class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/20 hidden md:!table-cell">{{ 'customer.dashboard.col_fulfillment' | t }}</th>
              <th class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/20 hidden md:!table-cell text-right">{{ 'customer.dashboard.col_total' | t }}</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {%- for order in customer.orders -%}
              {%- assign fulfillment = order.fulfillments.first -%}
              <tr class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[10px] leading-[1.8] text-bear-black">
                <td class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/10"><a href="{{ order.customer_url }}" class="font-bold hover-underline">{{ order.name }}</a></td>
                <td class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/10 whitespace-nowrap">{{ order.created_at | date: '%b %-d, %Y' }}</td>
                <td class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/10">
                  {%- if fulfillment.tracking_number -%}
                    {%- if fulfillment.tracking_url -%}<a href="{{ fulfillment.tracking_url }}" class="hover-underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ fulfillment.tracking_number }}</a>{%- else -%}{{ fulfillment.tracking_number }}{%- endif -%}
                  {%- else -%}&mdash;{%- endif -%}
                </td>
                <td class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/10 hidden md:!table-cell">{{ order.financial_status_label }}</td>
                <td class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/10 hidden md:!table-cell">{{ order.fulfillment_status_label }}</td>
                <td class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/10 hidden md:!table-cell text-right whitespace-nowrap">{{ order.total_price | money }}</td>
              </tr>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      {%- comment -%} The site's own pagination component (also used by product-grid and
        quick-order-list), not `default_pagination` — that filter emits bare browser-chrome links
        that looked nothing like the rest of the theme. The snippet self-styles and already
        returns nothing unless paginate.pages > 1, so a customer with 10 orders or fewer sees
        no control at all. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- render 'pagination-controls', paginate: paginate -%}
    {%- endpaginate -%}
  {%- elsif preview -%}
    {%- comment -%} PREVIEW-only mock table {%- endcomment -%}
    <div x-data="{ page: 1, per: 10, total: {{ mock_orders.size }}, get pages() { return Math.ceil(this.total / this.per) } }">
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      {%- comment -%} Same wb-orders-table class as the real table so the preview shows the real
        frame and header weight, not a lighter stand-in. {%- endcomment -%}
      <table class="w-full border-collapse wb-orders-table">
        <thead>
          <tr class="text-left tag text-bear-black uppercase">
            <th class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/20">{{ 'customer.dashboard.col_order' | t }}</th>
            <th class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/20">{{ 'customer.dashboard.col_date' | t }}</th>
            <th class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/20">{{ 'customer.dashboard.col_tracking' | t }}</th>
            <th class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/20 hidden md:!table-cell">{{ 'customer.dashboard.col_payment' | t }}</th>
            <th class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/20 hidden md:!table-cell">{{ 'customer.dashboard.col_fulfillment' | t }}</th>
            <th class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/20 hidden md:!table-cell text-right">{{ 'customer.dashboard.col_total' | t }}</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {%- for row in mock_orders -%}
            {%- assign c = row | strip | split: '|' -%}
            {%- comment -%} Alpine slices the rows client-side: Liquid cannot read ?page= and
              {% paginate %} only accepts Shopify objects, never a Liquid array. {%- endcomment -%}
            <tr x-show="Math.floor({{ forloop.index0 }} / per) + 1 === page"
                class="font-kurdis-semi-condensed font-bold text-[10px] leading-[1.8] text-bear-black">
              <td class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/10"><span class="font-bold hover-underline">{{ c[0] }}</span></td>
              <td class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/10 whitespace-nowrap">{{ c[1] }}</td>
              <td class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/10"><span class="hover-underline">{{ c[2] }}</span></td>
              <td class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/10 hidden md:!table-cell">{{ c[3] }}</td>
              <td class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/10 hidden md:!table-cell">{{ c[4] }}</td>
              <td class="px-2 py-3 md:!p-3 border-b border-espresso/10 hidden md:!table-cell text-right whitespace-nowrap">{{ c[5] }}</td>
            </tr>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
      {%- comment -%} Same DOM and class names as `pagination-controls` above, so the preview
        picks up that snippet's stylesheet and shows the real control rather than a stand-in.
        It cannot render the snippet itself: that needs a paginate object, and {% paginate %}
        only accepts Shopify objects, never a Liquid array. Hidden below two pages, matching
        the snippet's own `paginate.pages > 1` guard. {%- endcomment -%}
      <nav class="pagination" aria-label="{{ 'content.pagination.nav_label' | t }}" x-show="pages > 1">
        <ul class="pagination__list" role="list">
          <li class="pagination__item">
            <template x-if="page > 1">
              <a href="#" @click.prevent="page--" class="pagination__link pagination__link--arrow" aria-label="{{ 'content.pagination.previous' | t }}">{{ 'icon-chevron-left.svg' | inline_asset_content }}</a>
            </template>
            <template x-if="page === 1">
              <span class="pagination__link pagination__link--arrow pagination__link--disabled" aria-disabled="true" aria-label="{{ 'content.pagination.previous' | t }}">{{ 'icon-chevron-left.svg' | inline_asset_content }}</span>
            </template>
          </li>
          <template x-for="p in pages" :key="p">
            <li class="pagination__item">
              <template x-if="p !== page">
                <a href="#" @click.prevent="page = p" class="pagination__link pagination__link--page" x-text="p"></a>
              </template>
              <template x-if="p === page">
                <span class="pagination__link pagination__link--page pagination__link--current" aria-current="page" x-text="p"></span>
              </template>
            </li>
          </template>
          <li class="pagination__item">
            <template x-if="page < pages">
              <a href="#" @click.prevent="page++" class="pagination__link pagination__link--arrow" aria-label="{{ 'content.pagination.next' | t }}">{{ 'icon-chevron-right.svg' | inline_asset_content }}</a>
            </template>
            <template x-if="page === pages">
              <span class="pagination__link pagination__link--arrow pagination__link--disabled" aria-disabled="true" aria-label="{{ 'content.pagination.next' | t }}">{{ 'icon-chevron-right.svg' | inline_asset_content }}</span>
            </template>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </div>
  {%- else -%}
    <div class="text-center py-10">
      <p class="h3 text-espresso mb-2">{{ 'customer.dashboard.no_orders' | t }}</p>
      <p class="body text-espresso mb-5">{{ 'customer.dashboard.no_orders_sub' | t }}</p>
      {%- render 'wb-button', style: 'secondary-gold', label: t_shop, link: routes.all_products_collection_url, class: 'mx-auto !h-[43px] shrink-0' -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{%- comment -%} ---------- Contact CTA ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
<div class="relative">
  {%- comment -%} QA #34: Figma badge ("COLD BREW 96oz" group) is 101x91 and sits 33px above the
    card top on mobile — was 76px wide and pulled up by half its height, which left the heading
    crowded underneath. Width + offset + the card's mobile top padding live in account.css.
    z-[2], not z-20: the sticky header is z-index 8, and every ancestor here is position:relative
    with z-index:auto, which does NOT open a stacking context — so a 20 competed with the header
    directly and painted over it while scrolling. The badge only ever needed to beat its own
    sibling card, so 2 is enough. The credit-card labels use z-[1] for the same reason. {%- endcomment -%}
  <img src="{{ 'account-contact-badge.png' | asset_url }}" alt="Wandering Bear Cold Brew" width="120" height="120"
       class="wb-contact__badge absolute top-0 z-[2] w-[76px] smd:!w-[118px] h-auto left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 rotate-0 smd:!left-0 smd:!-translate-x-[20%] smd:!-translate-y-[20%] smd:!rotate-[-12deg]">
  <div class="wb-contact relative flex flex-col items-center justify-center overflow-hidden rounded-[10px] shadow-[0px_4px_4px_0px_rgba(0,0,0,0.25)] text-center px-6 py-6 smd:py-4 smd:aspect-[746/144] bg-cover bg-top bg-no-repeat bg-(--color-brand-light_cream)"
       style="background-image: url({{ 'account-contact-clouds.png' | asset_url }});">
    {%- comment -%} QA #33: Figma heading is 25px on mobile (1:177 / 1:466). {%- endcomment -%}
    <h2 class="font-kurdis-condensed font-extrabold uppercase text-espresso text-[25px] md:text-[28px] mb-2">{{ 'customer.dashboard.contact_title' | t }}</h2>
    <p class="body text-espresso mb-4">{{ 'customer.dashboard.contact_subtext' | t }}</p>
    {%- render 'wb-button', style: 'secondary-gold', label: t_contact, link: '/pages/contact', class: 'mx-auto !h-[43px] shrink-0' -%}
  </div>
</div>
